{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDD-Enterprises/dopemux-mvp/pulls/1227","id":4260977111,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPyIw9879-VnX","html_url":"https://github.com/DDD-Enterprises/dopemux-mvp/pull/1227","diff_url":"https://github.com/DDD-Enterprises/dopemux-mvp/pull/1227.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/DDD-Enterprises/dopemux-mvp/pull/1227.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDD-Enterprises/dopemux-mvp/issues/1227","number":1227,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"docs(second-brain): machine contracts for ADR acceptance evidence [READY_FOR_OPERATOR_MERGE_DECISION]","user":{"login":"hu3mann","id":167156098,"node_id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/167156098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hu3mann","html_url":"https://github.com/hu3mann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hu3mann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hu3mann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hu3mann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hu3mann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hu3mann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hu3mann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hu3mann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hu3mann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hu3mann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes the architecture-time machine-contract evidence gap blocking amended acceptance condition #2 for ADR-SB-001..010.\n\nBefore this change nothing in the repository could satisfy \"machine contracts required by this ADR MUST parse and cover the decision at ADR acceptance\": every ADR-named type (LocalSpoolPort, CustodyPort, OpenLoopCandidate, TaskProposal, TaskPromotionRequest, project identity envelope, service capability receipt) existed only as prose. That gap is reproduced and recorded in BASELINE_CONTRACT_INVENTORY.json before any artifact was authored.\n\nAdds a repository-owned contract family under schemas/second_brain/contracts/ — two meta-schemas, ten per-ADR contracts carrying 160 structured decision clauses, seven typed artifacts for the types the ADRs name directly, and a coverage matrix at 160/160 COVERED with MISSING=0 and AMBIGUOUS=0.\n\nThe coverage denominator is frozen in its own earlier commit, before any contract existed, so git history proves the freeze preceded authoring. Every clause binds verbatim fragments of the ratified candidate e4b28946..., machine-verified in both directions.\n\nA fail-closed validator (94 checks) and an adversarial matrix (63 tests executing the real validator against mutated repository copies) prove the evidence cannot false-green. Semantic mutations are applied consistently across inventory and contract, so a mutation that keeps the right shape and changes the architecture decision is still rejected.\n\nAlso reconciles the stale fo-01-repair-status.json against its later independent-verification receipt; the two records on main disagreed about whether FO-01 still blocked ADR acceptance.\n\nAccepts no ADR. All ten remain PROPOSED, the document remains CANDIDATE, SB-DEC-026 remains unlinked, and implementation execution remains NOT_AUTHORIZED. Denial fixtures remain an implementation-time gate and are explicitly not implemented.\n\n---\n\n**Round 2.** The first independent audit returned FAIL (3 blockers, 5 must-fix). The operator authorized re-freezing the coverage denominator and repairing the whole finding class in one wave. The denominator is now 160 clauses, frozen in its own commit under operator authorization and const-pinned in the validator; the second independent audit of frozen head 6e1b4472ba returned **PASS with 0 blockers and 0 must-fix**.\n\nRound-1 audit artifacts are unedited — they are the controlling evidence for why round 2 was required.\n\n**Post-#1228 rebind.** PR #1228 (`f0a0e839b4`) admitted `grok-cli` / `grok-4.5` on the trusted embedded-audit schema. This PR's proof metadata was rebound only: `embedded_audit` now states that identity from runner session evidence (`R2_AUDITOR_IDENTITY_RECONCILIATION.json`), without rewriting `AUDIT_PROMPT_CUSTODY_R2.json` or re-running the audit. The historical invocation is preserved without fabricating `-m`. Of the exact 36 C1 paths, the 31-file contract corpus remains byte-identical to `6e1b4472ba` (per-file blob hash); see `R2_AUDITED_BYTES_HASH_RECHECK.json`.\n\nGates that were red only for the representation gap are now green under the post-#1228 schema (embedded-audit hook, change-contract, pre-commit). Full proof corpus 76/76 PASS. Validator 94/94, adversarial suite 63/63.\n\nTerminal verdict: `READY_FOR_OPERATOR_CONTRACT_EVIDENCE_MERGE_DECISION`. Merge remains operator-only and conditional on final-head checks; no ADR disposition changes. Remote branch retention: `delete_branch_on_merge=false` on the repository before merge.\n","created_at":"2026-08-12T09:30:19Z","updated_at":"2026-08-13T17:36:52Z","closed_at":"2026-08-13T17:36:52Z","merged_at":"2026-08-13T17:36:52Z","merge_commit_sha":"75b4cfc581786a53445e412bfc8e25a6e0fdb978","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDD-Enterprises/dopemux-mvp/pulls/1227/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDD-Enterprises/dopemux-mvp/pulls/1227/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDD-Enterprises/dopemux-mvp/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDD-Enterprises/dopemux-mvp/issues/1227/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DDD-Enterprises/dopemux-mvp/statuses/da2523aafb6725be33f7bb69bc5eb50764d7394c","head":{"label":"DDD-Enterprises:tp/DMX-SB-ADR-CONTRACT-EVIDENCE-001","ref":"tp/DMX-SB-ADR-CONTRACT-EVIDENCE-001","sha":"da2523aafb6725be33f7bb69b